        <p>Pursuant to an Act of Parliament made and passed in the 22nd and 23rd years of the reign of her present Majesty Oap. 35 intituled "An Act to further amend the law ot Property and to relieve Trustees."</p>
        <p>NOTICE IS LIEREBY GIVEN THAT ALL C RED ITORS and P NINO NS HAVING ANY CLAIMS or Demands upon or against the estate of Arthur Evans late of The Cottage, Haydock, in the County of Lancaster and of 28 Bramham Gardens,Baris Court, South Kensington, in the County of Middlesex, Esquire. &amp;cease&amp; (who died on or about the 10th day of August 1236,and whose will was proved by William Harold Squire and Helen Squire the surviving executors named in the said will on the 23rd day of Novem- ber 1896 in the District egistry at Liverpool of the Probate Division of th High Court of Justice) are hereby required to- send the particulars of their claims and demands to the under- signed the solicitors of the said executors on or before the 9th day of Janu...:y 1897, and Notice is Hereby also Given that after that day the said executors will proceed to distribute the assets of the Deceased among the parties entitled thereto having regard only to the el kims of which the said executors than then have notice and that they will not be liable for the assets or any part thereof so distributed to any person of whose debt o: claim they shall not then have had notice. Dated this Bth day of December 1896.</p>
        <p>GEORUS lIADPIELD, BENNSTr &amp; CARLISLE, 20 bt. Ann's Square. Manchester. Solicitors for the Executors.</p>
        <p>RUNCORN UNION.-0001L AND LAUNDRESS. WANTED a SINGLE WOMAN or WIDOW without children dependent upon her to assist in Cooking and General Work at the Workhouse, Dutton. Wages £22 per annum with board,washing and lodging. Applications stating age and present and previous occupa- tion, accompanied by one or two testimonials. or ref eretoes, to be sent to me not later than Thursday the 17th instant. Further particulars as to the duties to be performed may be obtained on application to the MA ran at the Workhouse. The appointment wilt be made on TUESDAY the 22nd in- stant and selected candidates will receive Notice to attend on that day, and -third class return fares will be paid.</p>
