        <p>RAND XMAS U.-IM. (HANDSOME AND RELIABLE) FOR YOURSELF AND FRIENDS. Embrace this opportunity to secure a Lady's Magnificent Bright Silk JAPANESE ITEM-STITCHED HANDKERCHIEF In the following Colours : Indigo Rose, Lavender, Royol. Blue, Old Gold,Cerise Beret, Coral,Sky Blue,Cardinal, White, Mexico Blue. Having only a limited number shall be glad to receive orders as early as possible. PRICE, POST FREE PER REruRN is. 3D. SPECIAL CHRISTMAS OFrERS OF £45 IN FREE CASH PRIZES. First Prize, £l5 ; second, £lO ; third, £5; fourth. £3; fifth, £2 ; also a prize of £lO to the one sending the greatest number of orders (with remittance). THIS IS THOROUGHLY GENUINE. The above prizes are given to purchasers sending before the 27,rd of December only the most correct solutions of the following words, representing the names of seven welt • known great statesmen: B***** Is****D o.*** s*** E R*** B** y s* * * s** * y c** * * E****N H*** o**T P** N**L Instructions :—Fill in the star spaces (one letter in etch space) to represent the name of a well-known statesman. Copy those you find out on a sheet of paper and post it, together with P.O. or stamps for is. 3d.. and a stamned addressed envelope for prize result etc., to ROBERT CaEsx (Silk Mercer), 2 Gresham Buildings, Basingleill-strc3t, London, B.C. N.B.—This contest closes on December 23rd, 1896, bu' owing to the limited numbers, orders should b. sent as early as possible before then. Handker hie's will be despatchel per return. Prizes and results will be totted so as to reach competitors by Christmas Day. The prizes will be awarded in order of correctness. Should more than one send in col reet solution of all names, the money will be divided. I guarantee a prize to every person sending in all seven correct names. A letter is sent with Handkerchief stating whether your solutions are correct. THE PROOF .OF THE PUDDING IS IN THE BATING.</p>
